## 5. Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Measurable trigger | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Concurrent reservations create double bookings | Medium | High | Any production or concurrency-test case accepts overlapping reservations for one room | Use database exclusion constraints or serialisable transactions; test competing writes; monitor conflict and constraint-violation metrics |
| Legacy inventory database is slow or unavailable | High | Medium/High | Inventory query p95 exceeds 500 ms, or synchronisation is older than 15 minutes | Synchronise data into CLRS-owned storage; cache room metadata; display freshness status; retry with backoff |
| iCal feed format or availability changes unexpectedly | Medium | Medium | Parser errors exceed 1% of feed entries or feed has not updated for 30 minutes | Use tolerant, versioned parser; retain last-known valid feed; contract tests with representative feeds; alert facilities support |
| Kiosk updates exceed the ten-second requirement | Medium | High | FR-4 p95 exceeds ten seconds or outbox messages are older than 30 seconds | Use transactional outbox, retries, indexed room queries, SSE with polling fallback, local kiosk cache, and load testing |
| SAML configuration or claims differ between environments | Medium | High | Login failure rate exceeds 2% or required role claim is absent in staging | Obtain test IdP early; validate metadata and claims in CI/staging; maintain a documented emergency support process |
| Search performance fails at semester start | Medium | High | Load test p95 exceeds 400 ms or database CPU exceeds 70% at 2,000 users | Index time ranges and filters; cache static room data; precompute availability where useful; load-test before release; scale application instances |
| Notification provider delays or loses reminders | Medium | Medium | More than 1% of reminders are sent over two minutes late, or provider queue age exceeds five minutes | Use an outbox-backed notification worker, retries, provider monitoring, idempotency keys, and an operational report of failed reminders |
| A deployment or migration cannot be rolled back | Low/Medium | High | Rollback rehearsal takes over ten minutes or old version fails against the new schema | Use expand-and-contract migrations; immutable images; automated rollback; rehearse rollback before production |
| Two-person team lacks operational capacity | Medium | High | More than three unresolved high-severity alerts, or on-call response exceeds 15 minutes | Keep one deployable; automate CI/CD and backups; use managed infrastructure; create runbooks; limit first-release scope |
| Incorrect interpretation of block-booking notice rules | Medium | High | Product acceptance tests disagree with staff scenarios, or any block booking violates the agreed notice rule | Confirm policy with product owner; create example-based acceptance tests; require explicit override/audit workflow for exceptional cases |

